  <div class="pl-cards">
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>ArticleRepository.kt — route the sanitized query into the DAO MATCH call</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>The one-line correction: <code>searchWithScore</code> computes <code>sanitizedQuery</code> but hands the <em>raw</em> <code>query</code> to the DAO, so FTS sanitization/wildcards are silently discarded. Pass <code>sanitizedQuery</code> instead. Nothing else in the file changes — <code>sanitizeSearchQuery()</code>, <code>calculateScore()</code>, <code>delete()</code>, <code>add()</code>, and the constructor are untouched (those belong to app-scope / article-repository).</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "ctx", "text": "val sanitizedQuery = sanitizeSearchQuery(\"*$query*\")" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "articleDao.searchArticlesWithMatchInfo(query)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "articleDao.searchArticlesWithMatchInfo(sanitizedQuery)" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>FtsSearchTest.kt — pin the intended sanitized + wildcard/prefix semantics</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>New JVM unit test (MockK-stubbed <code>ArticleDao</code> + real <code>ArticleRepositoryImpl</code> on a <code>StandardTestDispatcher</code>; no Hilt/Room needed). Pins post-fix behaviour for every shape edge case via <code>coVerify { searchArticlesWithMatchInfo(expectedSanitized) }</code>.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "plain word        -> *\"*word*\"* reaches the DAO" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "unbalanced quote  -> internal quotes escaped, expression stays valid" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "lone * / AND/OR/NEAR -> escaped as literal text, no MATCH-operator leak" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "empty -> returns emptyList() without calling the DAO" },
          { "kind": "ctx", "text": "whitespace-only / non-ASCII -> non-crashing sanitized expression" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <!-- @include callout { "kind": "warn", "title": "Result-set change is intentional — not a regression", "body": "Routing the sanitized+wildcard query to the DAO changes which rows return for queries with FTS-special chars (quotes, <code>*</code>, AND/OR/NEAR). Reviewers must read any pre/post row diff as the <em>intended</em> correction. The new tests pin post-fix behaviour; pre-fix behaviour is deliberately not pinned." } -->
  <!-- @include callout { "kind": "info", "title": "Watch the double-wrap on wildcards", "body": "<code>searchWithScore</code> calls <code>sanitizeSearchQuery(\"*$query*\")</code>, which itself wraps in <code>*\"...\"*</code>. The edge-case tests confirm the composed expression is a valid FTS4 MATCH pattern and not overly broad/empty for typical queries." } -->
